{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T10:52:10.869Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-43p2c3+pm-5kfzjh+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-43p2c3","claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-43p2c3","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-9x9drr"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"pm package manage --fix-managed-state holds the extension state lock across every remote update lookup, so a raised update-check budget lengthens how long concurrent package actions wait"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Raised by CodeRabbit on PR 1752 (outside-diff comment on src/sdk/extension.ts, the prepareExploreManageState path). With --fix-managed-state, dispatchExtensionAction wraps the whole manage handler in withExtensionInstallLock. That handler adopts unmanaged packages and then calls refreshManagedExtensionUpdates, so the lock stays held while every npm view and git ls-remote runs, four at a time. The refresh never persists its result, so it does not need the lock. Behaviour is unchanged at the default 10-second budget, but PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS (pm-5kfzjh) can raise each lookup to 120 seconds. A concurrent install, uninstall or adopt then waits longer for the lock and can fail with a lock conflict. Proposed: keep only the adoption read and write under the lock, and run the refresh and runtime probe after it is released."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["concurrency","extensions","locking","update-check"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-18T10:52:10.869Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T10:52:10.869Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"manage --fix-managed-state holds the extension state lock only for the adoption read and write; the remote update refresh and runtime probe run after the lock is released, with the same results and offline behaviour; a test proves a concurrent locked package action is not blocked by a slow lookup; manage without --fix-managed-state is unchanged"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A slow or long-budget update lookup never holds the extension state lock"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"With --fix-managed-state the lock spans every remote update lookup, up to the configured budget per lookup"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"extensions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-5kfzjh","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-18T10:52:10.869Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"4265ed640a8d0ff273da5309d35dbe8e7fd34ff2863f3fb55